      },
      "message": "fix(#622): pole clicks snap the roll to the nearest quarter turn\n\nAt an exact Z pole toward() read atan2(0,0)=0 and basis_right pinned\nscreen-right to literal +X, so clicking TOP/BOT spun a yawed view up to\nhalf a turn on screen. Now the pole takes the pre-click yaw snapped to\nthe nearest FRAC_PI_2, and basis_right's zero-guard evaluates\n(-sin y, cos y, 0) at that yaw - the limit every near-pole view already\nrides, so the guard is continuous and a second pole click is a no-op.\ndocs/decisions/622-viewcube-roll-snap.md.",
      "tree": {
